# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env itself.
#
# This file only lists what's needed before the app can even reach its own
# database (UI_HOST/UI_PORT/UI_DB_PATH), infrastructure endpoints an
# operator might need to point somewhere non-default (the MQTT broker
# host, SENAPRED's Cognito/AppSync identity — only used once, to seed a
# fresh database, see below), and secrets. Every other setting —
# dispatcher/actions/beacon tuning, MQTT topics, beacon type/output/
# templates/voice/AX.25/TTS config, display timezone, UI page size/
# refresh intervals/dev-tools toggle, etc. — is edited live, with no
# restart, from the running app's /config page (backed by
# ui/src/ui/config_catalog.py's SETTINGS_CATALOG), not here. Every one of
# those settings still honors an identically-named env var if you set one
# (see adapters.storage.get_setting's resolution order: DB row -> env var
# -> hardcoded default) — this file just no longer documents each one
# individually, since /config's own descriptions are the single source of
# truth for defaults now. Which data adapters exist, their type (API vs
# CUSTOM), and their own fetch config/poll interval live in a separate
# table entirely, edited at /adapters — see data-adapters/README.md.
#
# Naming convention: vars specific to one adapter are prefixed with the
# adapter's name (e.g. ADAPTERS_SENAPRED_*); generic vars (used across
# adapters, or read directly by a third-party SDK under its own standard
# name) have no prefix.

# --- Bootstrap (ui.config) — needed before the UI can open the database
# at all, so these can never be DB-backed like every other setting. ---

# Host/port ui/start.sh binds to. Defaults to 0.0.0.0 (all interfaces) —
# NOTE there is no auth, and every action is an unauthenticated POST, so
# only run it on a trusted network. Set UI_HOST=127.0.0.1 to take it off
# the network, or put auth (a reverse proxy) in front of it.
# UI_HOST=0.0.0.0
UI_PORT=8080

# Comma-separated Host-header allow-list (DNS-rebinding guard) and the
# origins allowed to submit the dashboard's forms. Defaults to "*" (guard
# off). Narrow it to the exact names/IPs you serve under to re-arm the
# guard — a Host not listed then gets a 400.
# UI_ALLOWED_HOSTS=127.0.0.1,localhost,shack.local,192.168.1.10

# Path to radiobeacon.db. Leave unset to use the same default every other
# package uses (adapters.storage.DEFAULT_DB_PATH, storage/radiobeacon.db).
# UI_DB_PATH=

# --- MQTT broker hosts — all three default to localhost (the broker
# mq/start.sh brings up; see mq/README.md), so leave these commented for a
# normal setup. Set one to a hostname to point at a remote broker, or to
# an empty string (e.g. DISPATCHER_MQ_HOST=) to disable that package's MQTT
# entirely. Port/QoS/timeout for each is DB-editable via /config once the
# app is running. ---
# DISPATCHER_MQ_HOST=localhost
# ACTIONS_MQ_HOST=localhost
# BEACON_MQ_HOST=localhost

# --- SENAPRED adapter identity/AWS plumbing — public, non-secret values
# reverse-engineered from senapred.cl's own JS bundle (see the "senapred"
# instance's seeded code at data-adapters/src/adapters/storage.py). Only
# read ONCE, the very first time a fresh database is created (folded into
# the seeded adapter_instances row so this file can still customize it
# ahead of first boot) — after that, edit the running senapred instance's
# config directly at /adapters, not here; changing these vars later has
# no effect. ---
ADAPTERS_SENAPRED_IDENTITY_POOL_ID=us-east-1:17c696bc-53e1-49a2-991f-f1b65f752fda
ADAPTERS_SENAPRED_COGNITO_REGION=us-east-1
ADAPTERS_SENAPRED_APPSYNC_REGION=us-east-1
ADAPTERS_SENAPRED_APPSYNC_HOST=rz2uv7ifxbgflh2bqmp6kmh4le.appsync-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com

# --- Secrets (actions.ai) — only used if you set ACTIONS_AI_ENABLED=true
# and pick a provider via /config. Never committed; leave unset unless
# you're using that provider. ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
